      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-10-22T18:39:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "why is the copy size different than line 538?\n\nwhat is the reserved field being used for? What if upstream uses the reserved field for something else -- this looks risky.",
      "revId": "8f33c492a28a9028ebde7dfe9fbb34e16788cdb6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4d454b89_58d17fab",
        "filename": "drivers/media/v4l2-core/v4l2-compat-ioctl32.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 504,
      "author": {
        "id": 1584147
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-10-23T19:46:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I will update p64-\u003elength with p64-\u003ereserved.\n\nreserved field is used for passing extra information (mark_data or buffer_tag etc) along with the buffer to driver. Current QCOM video driver needs this fix.\n\n64 bit clients passing reserved fields to video driver but 32 bit clients are not able to pass because copy_in_user() not available for reserved fields in this function.\n\nIf upstream uses reserved fields then video driver functionality will be broken with that kernel upgrade and it will be fixed in video driver.\n\nBut I believe by the time upstream uses this field QCOM video userspace and driver will be modified and will be upstream compliant to not use reserved fields.",
      "parentUuid": "2f1f1d17_a5b96398",
      "revId": "8f33c492a28a9028ebde7dfe9fbb34e16788cdb6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "30632187_13c9c6e3",
        "filename": "drivers/media/v4l2-core/v4l2-compat-ioctl32.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 504,
      "author": {
        "id": 1069543
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-10-23T20:18:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is there a reason these changes to the video driver can\u0027t be made now to avoid using the reserved field?\n\n\u003e by the time upstream uses this field...\n\nThis is the android-mainline branch which gets updates from linux mainline on every RC. So if upstream changes it in 5.4-rc4, this code will be broken in android-mainline a few days later.\n\nSince this *is* upstream, the code needs to be upstream compliant in this way.",
      "parentUuid": "4d454b89_58d17fab",
      "revId": "8f33c492a28a9028ebde7dfe9fbb34e16788cdb6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "29b6497f_901223ba",
        "filename": "drivers/media/v4l2-core/v4l2-compat-ioctl32.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 504,
      "author": {
        "id": 1584147
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-10-23T20:42:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It seems there is no way to pass extra information to driver along with buffer (synchronously) other than using reserved fields.",
      "parentUuid": "30632187_13c9c6e3",
      "revId": "8f33c492a28a9028ebde7dfe9fbb34e16788cdb6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ab544651_11be1d48",
        "filename": "drivers/media/v4l2-core/v4l2-compat-ioctl32.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 504,
      "author": {
        "id": 1584147
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-10-23T21:15:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is bug in v4l2 framework code.\n\nFor 64 bit client (and 64 bit kernel) the reserved fields are copied from clients to driver.\nWhere as 32 bit client is not able to pass reserved fields. This is a bug in v4l2 framework which we are fixing with this change.\n\nThis bug is not related to whether client or driver is using reserved fields.\nWe are using 32 bit userspace due to Google\u0027s mediaserver restriction. \nIn fact we would like switch to 64 bit userspace if Android can move mediaserver process to 64 bit.\n\nHaving said that we will look at the feasibility of not using reserved fields in future.\nBut after quick analysis it seems not using reserved fields in non-trivial and needs much more design changes in both Qcom userspace and driver.\n\nHence overall I would request you review this change with this background details.\nLet us know if you would like to have a quick call for this change.",
      "parentUuid": "29b6497f_901223ba",
      "revId": "8f33c492a28a9028ebde7dfe9fbb34e16788cdb6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cbca59e9_75671bce",
        "filename": "drivers/media/v4l2-core/v4l2-compat-ioctl32.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 538,
      "author": {
        "id": 1069543
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-10-23T20:18:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "are we sure that sizeof(p32-\u003ereserved) \u003d\u003d sizeof(p64-\u003ereserved) always? Is there a chance that this overruns p32-\u003ereserved?",
      "revId": "8f33c492a28a9028ebde7dfe9fbb34e16788cdb6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "831fc77d_d54ce42c",
        "filename": "drivers/media/v4l2-core/v4l2-compat-ioctl32.c",
